; The browser artifact. Same extracted core as the native build, compiled to
; JavaScript, so there is one implementation rather than two.
;
; zarith_stubs_js supplies pure-JS implementations of Zarith's C primitives;
; without it the extracted core's bignum arithmetic has no backing in a browser.
(executable
 (name tessarium_js)
 (modes js)
 (libraries tessarium tessarium_extracted zarith zarith_stubs_js js_of_ocaml)
 (preprocess (pps js_of_ocaml-ppx))
 ; No source map. Under dune's dev profile js_of_ocaml inlines one. It was
 ; 2,924 KB of a 5,106 KB bundle, and 68% of that bundle's gzipped weight,
 ; because a source map is text and compresses no better. Disabled here rather
 ; than by building this one executable under --profile release, so that the
 ; bundle the tests run against is byte-identical to the bundle that ships.
 ;
 ; whole_program: dune's dev default links each library separately, which
 ; keeps every module whether the browser reaches it or not. yojson, stdint
 ; and ppx_deriving arrive through ocaml/fstarlib, which tessarium_extracted
 ; depends on; the browser calls none of them. Compiling the whole program at
 ; once lets js_of_ocaml drop what nothing calls.
 (js_of_ocaml (sourcemap no) (compilation_mode whole_program)))
